        "reply_text": "I understand you purchased a phone charger for 800 rupees in October 2026, but it is not working. You have the bill and have already contacted support without success.\n\nUnder the law, you may bring a product liability action against a product seller or manufacturer if you have suffered harm due to a defective product.\n\nA manufacturer can be held liable if the product has a manufacturing defect, a design defect, or does not conform to an express warranty.\n\nYou can register your grievance at the pre-litigation stage through the National Consumer Helpline (NCH) by calling 1915. You can also use the INGRAM portal (consumerhelpline.gov.in), the NCH app, or send a message via WhatsApp to 8800001915.\n\nIf the issue is not resolved, you may file a formal complaint with the District Commission.\n\nKeep your bill and any records of your communication with the seller's support team in a safe place.\n\nPlease provide the name of the company or seller and the specific model or brand of the charger so I can provide more relevant information.\n\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 83\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 84\nSource: National Consumer Helpline Grievance Redressal Procedure, procedure 1\nSource: National Consumer Helpline Guidelines, helpline 1915\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 35\n\nWhat I could not verify:\n- specific procedures for filing a complaint at the District Commission in Uttar Pradesh\n- legal advice on whether your specific situation qualifies for a refund or replacement\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
